WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.280
The fifth episode of Game of Thrones' eighth
and final season was many things.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.360
Tense and cinematic?

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.160
Yup.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.560
Full of shots that looked straight out of
an action movie?

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:09.220
Oh yeah.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.380
But the penultimate episode left us with one
burning question:

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.040
[DRAGON FIIIIIIIIIIIIIRE]

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.460
Who will take the Iron Throne now?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:18.520
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.620
There's no nice way to describe the most recent
episode of Game of Thrones.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.920
Daenerys Targaryen attacked King's Landing
and set the city ablaze, and she refused to

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.020
back down even after Cersei's army surrendered.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.380
[Cersei’s army surrendering, unaware they
are about to be massacred anyway]

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.240
Thousands of innocent people were burnt to
a crisp by Drogon's fire, or slaughtered by

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.190
Daenerys' Unsullied soldiers and Dothraki
riders.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.940
It was, in a word, brutal.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.680
Until she stormed King's Landing, Daenerys
looked poised to become the new ruler of the

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.560
Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.380
Because she's the daughter of Aerys Targaryen
- otherwise known as The Mad King - she's

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.860
always had a claim to queenship.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.451
Over the years, Daenerys has proven she has
what it takes to rule: strength, compassion

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.240
where it counts, and bias for bloodshed when
necessary.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.719
But she's also killed without mercy in the
past, and she hasn't always strategized wisely

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:05.210
without the guidance of her counsel.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.440
Her behavior on the latest episode threatens
to undo all of her past triumphs.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.580
Many fans are convinced she took a free-fall
when she destroyed King's Landing, and there's

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.460
no way she'll ever be able to redeem herself.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.060
Unless she can persuade the rest of Westeros
to bend the knee and recognize her as Queen,

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.710
there's a good chance she won't fulfill her
deepest desire to sit on the Iron Throne as

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.740
her father once did.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.960
That brings us to Jon Snow.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.080
He's the legitimate heir to the Iron Throne,
but he's made his feelings on the matter quite

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:31.580
clear.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:32.640
"I don't want it.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.780
I never have.”

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.340
He bent the knee to Daenerys before either
of them knew his true parentage, and so far

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.540
he's remained loyal to her.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.020
But perhaps there's more at play here, particularly
since Jon had his brother-cousin Bran Stark

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.280
inform his sister-cousins Arya and Sansa of
his heritage.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:52.560
Sansa then told Tyrion Lannister, who told
Varys, who was subsequently executed.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:56.440
Jon probably didn't know he'd set off this
chain of events, but other people might think

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.840
it was all a deliberate ploy.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.000
Some fans think Jon will be forced to kill
Daenerys, thus ending her reign of terror.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.020
He'd take the Iron Throne against his true
desires, but for the greater good of his people.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.440
That would certainly fulfill the vision Daenerys
had back in season 2, in which Dany envisioned

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.840
herself walking through the throne room, looking
up to see the ceiling torn apart, then approaching

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.520
an Iron Throne that was covered in snow.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.160
After watching this most recent episode, many
believe the snow is actually ash, but what

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.660
if her vision represented Jon Snow taking
the Throne?

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:29.020
If Jon doesn't seize the Iron Throne, another
force from the North could: Sansa.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.120
She's a keen political strategist.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.850
And she has no trouble delivering justice
when it's required.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.700
"Thank you for all your many lessons, Lord
Baelish.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.020
I will never forget them."

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.440
Her childhood spent in King's Landing under
the watchful eyes of Cersei Lannister forced

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:48.210
her to grow up quickly, turning her into one
of the smartest, most compassionate people

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:48.900
in a room.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.200
Though her heart has remained with Winterfell
and the North, she began Game of Thrones wanting

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.480
to serve as Queen alongside King Joffrey more
than anything.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.840
Perhaps a part of her is still holding onto
that dream.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.960
We last saw Arya riding on the back of a pale
horse, badly wounded and escaping the rubble

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:04.820
of King's Landing.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.600
Maybe she's on her way to kill Daenerys.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.950
Or maybe she's making her way back to Winterfell
to warn everyone that Dany has really lost

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:11.540
it this time.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:16.380
Arya has exhibited many characteristics of
a strong leader: determination, cunning, and

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.520
compassion for others.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.060
Some fans think Arya will kill Dany and then
put her training at the House of Black and

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.360
White to good use, ruling Westeros using someone
else's face.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.880
Then again, that would contradict Arya's previous
statement to Gendry:

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.340
"I'm not a lady.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.400
I never have been.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:35.840
That's not me."

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:37.880
Consider Bran.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.020
As wild as it sounds, he could genuinely take
the Iron Throne.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.320
He's technically not even Bran Stark anymore.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.160
He's the Three-Eyed Raven, and he uses his
powerful gifts to keep people well-informed

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.100
and well-prepared.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.580
Tyrion Lannister once told Bran he'd make
an excellent leader, and Bran seemed to cryptically

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.800
suggest he had no desire for the Throne.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.790
"I don't really want anymore."

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.540
A lot of fans are putting their money on Bran
because of a remark Varys made about who should

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.580
oversee Westeros:

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.140
"Have you considered the best ruler might
be someone who doesn't want to rule?"

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.180
To guide them into a brighter future, people
will want someone new and unlike any other

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.380
ruler they've seen before.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:15.840
And who better to teach future generations
about history than an entity that can access

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.960
more information than anyone else in the world?

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.880
The final major contender for the Iron Throne
is Tyrion Lannister.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.120
He's certainly proven capable in politics.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.460
And he remains the Hand of the Queen to Daenerys,
even if he's realizing that she's in no position

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:28.960
to rule.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.260
If Dany dies in the series finale, Tyrion
will arguably be the most politically-savvy

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.620
character left standing.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.980
He's fought in battles.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.800
He's masterminded war strategies.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:41.600
While advising kings and queens, he's learned
that ruling isn't all about extremes.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.940
Plus, he's saved King's Landing before - in
the Battle of the Blackwater.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.990
That means there's a good chance he can prevent
further drama down the road if he takes the

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:49.480
throne.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:53.280
When it comes right down to it, there's a
distinct possibility that no one will sit

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.080
on the Iron Throne.

00:04:54.281 --> 00:04:58.080
Perhaps the sacred seat corrupts anyone who
takes it, and the song of ice and fire was

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:00.730
meant to end on a hollow note, and with an
empty chair.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.190
As we've seen before, absolutely anything
can happen on this show.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.740
For now, all we can do is wait.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.180
The answer will be revealed when the final
episode of Game of Thrones airs.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.020
Godspeed!

